{
  "title": "Etiquettes of the Asr Prayer",
  "data": "Upon accomplishment of the post-prayer utterances, you may ready yourself for performing the Afternoon (Asr) Prayer.\nYou may begin with offering the Supererogatory Afternoon Prayer, which consists of eight units.\nUpon accomplishment, you may perform the Afternoon Obligatory Prayer, observing all the [etiquettes of prayer](I7).\nIt is highly advisable to recite [Surah al-Faatehah](A5) and [Surah al-Nasr](A114) (No. 110), [Surah al-Fath](A52) (No. 48), [Surah al-Takathur](A106) (No. 102), or a similar Surah in the first unit and [Surah al-Faatehah](A5) and [Surah al-Tawheed](A116) in the second.\nUpon accomplishment, you may say any of the [general post-prayer supplicatory utterances](I9) and the other supplications dedicated to the Afternoon Prayer, such as imploring Almighty Allah’s forgiveness seventy times and repeating [Surah al-Qadr](A101) ten times.\nYou may then do the thanksgiving prostration."
}
